  "preamble": "A prothetic [i] is added before a word-initial consonant cluster in languages that do not allow clusters at the start of a word. Hungarian borrowed Latin schola as iskola. In Arabic, a prothetic i- (hamzat al-waṣl) appears before an initial cluster when the word begins an utterance, as in ism 'name' and ibn 'son'.",
